Compat before-patch for b6d536-e7a-repaired-b15-refresh, applied to f648453b5 (the parent of the
E7a lane commit 481434f82; coordinator decision 4, lane-parent route with add-only patches).

NativeSessionHandlePlannedFp32Test now also holds checks that name the device-memory plan API
(added with 481434f82 and extended in 7de3976a1), so the file did not compile on f648453b5. This
patch adds only declarations with immediate no-op returns: GpuArenaPlan (Facts, Settings,
Settings.none, resolve), DeviceArenaPlans (publish, withdraw), GpuCallPacker.itemsPerCall,
NativeSessionHandle.arenaPlan() (empty), and a test-side GpuArenaPlanTest holding only the two
helpers the file names (facts, STANDARD_ONLY). No production code in this state reads any of them,
and the named check aFailedFp16CreationOnAPlannedProfileDoesNotLoadTheFp32FileOnTheGpu calls none
of them: its planned() helper already falls back by reflection to the before-state policy.

